        "In January 1906 a small holiness church from the mountains of North Carolina and Tennessee, led by the former Quaker Bible salesman A. J. Tomlinson, holds its first General Assembly; in 1907 it takes the name Church of God and settles in Cleveland, Tennessee. In 1908, after the Pentecostal preacher G. B. Cashwell visits, Tomlinson speaks in tongues and the church becomes Pentecostal. The Church of God (Cleveland) grew into one of the largest Pentecostal denominations, with millions of members in Latin America, the Caribbean and Africa.",
