        "In September 1941 Carl McIntire, the Bible Presbyterian pastor of Collingswood, New Jersey, and a former student of Machen, founds the American Council of Christian Churches as a separatist fundamentalist rival to the liberal-leaning Federal Council of Churches; in 1948 he added the International Council of Christian Churches. McIntire's militant separatism and radio broadcasts against modernism and communism influenced fundamentalist churches in Latin America, and his refusal to cooperate pushed moderate conservatives to form the National Association of Evangelicals.",
