        "In 1947 Oral Roberts, a Pentecostal Holiness pastor in Enid, Oklahoma, launches a healing ministry and moves to Tulsa, soon preaching under one of the largest gospel tents in the world. He was a leading figure of the post-war healing revival, and from 1955 he took his crusades onto television, bringing Pentecostal worship into millions of homes. In 1963 he opened Oral Roberts University in Tulsa. His teaching of 'seed-faith' giving made him a forerunner of the prosperity gospel, widely influential — and much debated — in Latin America.",
